---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---
<Page wide>
<section class="hero">
  <img src="/riverhorse.png" alt="Riverhorse" width="160" height="160">
  <h1>Riverhorse</h1>
  <p class="tagline">A PlayStation emulator that starts straight into the game.</p>
  <p class="lede">Accurate PS1 emulation for Linux, Windows, macOS and RetroArch, with rollback netplay, save sync between devices and an interface you can drive with a controller. It runs well on low-end ARM handhelds too.</p>
  <p class="cta"><a class="button primary" href="#download">Download</a> <a class="button" href="/docs">Get started</a></p>
</section>

<section class="features">
  <article>
    <h2>Accurate</h2>
    <p>CD-ROM timing modelled on hardware measurements, reworked GPU, SPU, DMA, MDEC and GTE timing, and extended PGXP geometry correction.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>Rollback netplay</h2>
    <p>Up to four players and four spectators. Join with a session code or from the public session list.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>Save sync</h2>
    <p>Memory cards, save states and game settings follow you between devices through a synced folder or a WebDAV server.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>Looks great</h2>
    <p>Software, OpenGL, Vulkan, Direct3D and Metal renderers, upscaling, widescreen and 60 FPS patches, shaders and bezels.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>Made for the couch</h2>
    <p>A fullscreen interface with cover shelves, Continue Playing and an in-game side panel, and themes for dark, light and high contrast.</p>
  </article>
  <article>
    <h2>Cheats and patches</h2>
    <p>About 66,000 cheats for over 1,900 games, plus fix patches, and your own patches per game.</p>
  </article>
</section>

<section id="download" class="download">
  <h2>Download</h2>
  <p>The latest release is on <a href="https://github.com/thenotoriousfox/riverhorse/releases/latest">GitHub</a>. You also need a BIOS dumped from your own console; see <a href="/docs#bios">BIOS</a>.</p>
  <div class="platforms">
    <div class="platform">
      <h3>Linux</h3>
      <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/thenotoriousfox/riverhorse/releases/latest/download/Riverhorse-x64.AppImage">AppImage (x64)</a>
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/thenotoriousfox/riverhorse/releases/latest/download/Riverhorse-arm64.AppImage">AppImage (ARM64)</a>
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/thenotoriousfox/riverhorse/releases/latest/download/riverhorse-x64.flatpak">Flatpak (x64)</a>
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/thenotoriousfox/riverhorse/releases/latest/download/riverhorse-arm64.flatpak">Flatpak (ARM64)</a>
    </div>
    <div class="platform">
      <h3>Windows</h3>
      <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/thenotoriousfox/riverhorse/releases/latest/download/riverhorse-windows-x64-release.zip">Windows (x64)</a>
      <a class="button" href="https://github.com/thenotoriousfox/riverhorse/releases/latest/download/riverhorse-windows-arm64-release.zip">Windows (ARM64)</a>
    </div>
    <div class="platform">
      <h3>macOS</h3>
      <a class="button primary" href="https://github.com/thenotoriousfox/riverhorse/releases/latest/download/riverhorse-mac-release.zip">macOS</a>
    </div>
    <div class="platform">
      <h3>libretro core</h3>
      <p>For RetroArch and other libretro frontends, on Linux, Windows, Android and macOS. Pick your platform from the <a href="https://github.com/thenotoriousfox/riverhorse/releases/latest">release page</a> (<code>riverhorse_libretro-&lt;platform&gt;.zip</code>) and see <a href="/docs#libretro-core">installing the core</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Page>
